# Mooneye test-suite harness.
#
# Each Mooneye ROM ends by executing `LD B, B` (opcode $40) as a "test
# complete" marker after computing its result.  On pass it sets the
# Fibonacci fingerprint B=3, C=5, D=8, E=13, H=21, L=34 — see the
# Mooneye howto: <C:\code\emu\gb-test-roms\mooneye-test-suite\
# game-boy-test-roms-howto.md>.
#
# `run-until ld-b-b` stops on that opcode; `dump regs` writes the live
# register line to the output file; CTest's EXPECT regex matches the
# pass fingerprint substring "BC=0305 DE=080D HL=1522".  A fail test
# lands on the same LD B, B with non-Fibonacci registers, so the regex
# misses and ctest reports a fail.
#
# Mooneye's reference runner allows up to 120 emulated seconds per test
# (~500M T-cycles).  Most tests finish in well under 1M cycles, so the
# generous safety cap below only matters for a runaway emulator bug.
run-until ld-b-b max-cycles 500000000
dump regs
exit
